            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for fortune, then the Latin for an accident."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: aurum, aurī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aurum, aurī — \"gold\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aurum is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European h2eh2usom, \"a glow\", from h2ews-, \"to dawn, to grow light\" (EtymDB 2.1), the root of aurōra, \"dawn\". Festus records a Sabine ausum, \"gold\", which keeps the older s (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
